{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EVfBa1Nqgu8te3XXJ5FkBW","type":"tool_result","content":"[package]\nname = \"translation\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\nname = \"normalize_lib\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n# This crate is a byte-for-byte ABI-compatible replacement for a C library, so\n# it must reproduce the C behaviour even for inputs that are UB in both\n# languages (NULL pointers, negative sizes). rustc's debug-assertion UB checks\n# turn a NULL dereference into a Rust `abort()` (SIGABRT) where the C code\n# faults (SIGSEGV), which is an observable divergence, so they are off in every\n# profile.\n[profile.dev]\ndebug-assertions = false\noverflow-checks = false\n\n[profile.test]\ndebug-assertions = false\noverflow-checks = false\n\n[profile.release]\npanic = \"abort\"\ndebug-assertions = false\noverflow-checks = false\n\n[workspace]\n=== warnings check ===\n  Executable tests/error_paths.rs (target/debug/deps/error_paths-b973e07e328eca51)\n(no output above = clean)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60ecd44c-7cf3-43cb-a7b9-fdde59ad8684","uuid":"27d681ab-8911-4dbc-8e58-ca0b2959ddd7","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:31:24.181Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"[package]\nname = \"translation\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\nname = \"normalize_lib\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n# This crate is a byte-for-byte ABI-compatible replacement for a C library, so\n# it must reproduce the C behaviour even for inputs that are UB in both\n# languages (NULL pointers, negative sizes). rustc's debug-assertion UB checks\n# turn a NULL dereference into a Rust `abort()` (SIGABRT) where the C code\n# faults (SIGSEGV), which is an observable divergence, so they are off in every\n# profile.\n[profile.dev]\ndebug-assertions = false\noverflow-checks =